# Sub-tick corpus for the terrain env-anim colour path (terrain-canim). Row
# grammar and what the statistic means: see
# games/spyro-1/corpus/terrain-canim-subtick-corpus.manifest.
#
# No movie in this game's corpus visits a level whose colour sub-list is
# populated: sunrise_spring, sheilas_alp, icy_peak, crystal_islands and
# spikes_arena name 0 sectors on it. Evening Lake names 5; the row boots it
# with --skip-to-level and holds a freecam above the lake sectors, where the
# legs separate by 6438 px at alpha 1, a mean step of 1.18 levels, and the
# retained cache draws 6 of the animated sectors (the capture under
# OPENPETE_TERRAIN_CACHE_FORCE=1 is pixel-identical to the walk's).
#
# The row reads PARTIAL (alpha 0.5: 0.25 levels from the lerp, ratio 0.42;
# alpha 0.25 differs in 0 px): the lake's per-tick steps are 1-5 levels per
# channel, and the lerped words sit on the RGB888 grid the terrain colour path
# carries, so a 1-level step reads 0 below alpha 0.5 and 1 from it. The row is
# kept out of the ctest list until that path carries fractional colour.
evening-lake | 2973 | level=evening_lake pose=36800,70400,40000,0,992
